// "Low Sun": a drop-D piece at 88, in D minor, fifty-two bars, about two minutes and twenty
// seconds. Original music, written here, by Claude for Ryan. The brief: "a sick drop D guitar
// riff reminiscent of the Deftones", then, of the first version, "more math rock". Nothing of
// any recording or score is quoted.
//
// What it is for: to hear engine::guitar play a piece. Mood: heavy, hazy, patient.
//
// An ear's notes on the first version (twenty-five bars; a riff of chugs in threes with
// chords on F, E flat and D): too short, and it doesn't develop; the riff is generic ("short
// chunky riffs have to be memorable if they're gonna be played; otherwise big walls of
// guitars with long power chords are better"); the middle section, the tune and its
// atmosphere, is the best part; and, of the second mix, the drums and the bass are still low.
//
// So, this version:
// - the riff is a seven-sixteenth cell said against a straight four: the open low chord, a
//   run of two notes up, and a landing on the octave, then a rest. Said three times in two
//   bars, its landing a half step high the second time; the fourth time it climbs the wrong
//   way (F, A flat, C) and two long chords, B flat and C, turn it round. The drums keep a
//   plain backbeat under it, so the sevens roll over the bar line and reset every two bars;
// - everywhere else the heavy guitars play walls: chords of a fifth held one and two bars;
// - the middle is twice as long: the tune as it was, then the walls come in under it and it
//   climbs to its one highest note, a ninth over C, held; the riff cuts in on the bar line
//   and D makes that note its root;
// - it develops: the figure alone; the bass joins it; the riff; the tune; the tune over the
//   walls; the riff with an octave ringing over it; the walls with the tune's first words;
//   the figure alone again;
// - the drums and the bass are up, the guitars down and pushed down a little more by each
//   bass drum, and the master is driven less, so the drums' hits aren't flattened.
//
// An ear's notes on the second version (the riff a seven-sixteenth cell running up D minor's
// five notes to the octave): "the most bland ass riff ever. It sounds like mom rock. I want
// it fucking dark. I want it to go hard." A run up the pentatonic to the octave is classic
// rock's own figure, whatever it is counted in. The riff now is on the low strings alone:
// muted chugs on the open string, a stab a half step over it, the tritone left hanging, and
// a fall home by half steps that stops dead; the drums strike every stroke with it. The
// closing walls go to E flat, a half step over home, and not to C. The sevens are gone.
//
// An ear's notes on the third version (chugs on the open string, a stab a half step over
// it, a hanging tritone, a fall by half steps, the bass drum on every stroke): "No. Rocket
// Skates by the Deftones is heavy. Jesus Glue by Glassjaw is heavy. This is bland and
// weird." What those two do, researched (tabs read as data): each riff is one short cell of
// three or four pitches said over and over; one has three strokes and then a whole beat of
// silence, the other a note on the low string pushed up a half step from the tritone; the
// snare is once a bar on its third beat, so the backbeat is at half speed; the bass drum
// and a crash strike with the guitar and nothing fills the gaps; the bass holds or doubles.
// A riff of fast chugs under moving chords fills every gap and exposes no stroke: the
// opposite. The riff now: the open chord twice, the tritone bent up to the fifth and held;
// the open chord twice and a beat of nothing. Sixths of a beat, not quarters of it.
//
// The spine, from the listener's taste (the music skill's taste sheet): withhold, then drop
// in whole (no drums for eight bars; half a bar of near silence; then everyone on one
// downbeat, no fill); a rolling figure as the bed (sixteenths in threes against four over two
// notes that never change, an echo a dotted eighth behind); a short loop with no dominant (D,
// B flat with its major seventh, C); a tune that hovers on two neighbouring notes, each said
// twice, then leaps and holds; the bass as a character (alone with the figure, with a line
// of its own); the cut is the resolution.
//
// The style, researched before writing (tabs read as data, interviews, lessons): their heavy
// riffs are one finger across the low strings against the open low chord, one or two bars
// long; the fretted notes are mostly a half step or a step from the open one or each other,
// and land off the beat; octave shapes ring over the open string. The snare is tuned high and
// dry, on beat 3 alone in the half-time ones, with ghost notes; the bass plays in unison. A
// quiet section is a clean guitar on two chords a major third apart. Their records are in
// lower tunings than drop D. The sevens are not theirs: they are the math in "math rock",
// and near the listener's own list (threes against four that roll over the bar line).
//
// The form, with each section's energy (1 to 10):
//   bars 1-4     the figure alone                                   2
//   bars 5-8     the bass joins it                                  3
//   bars 9-16    the riff, everyone                                 9
//   bars 17-24   the figure, held chords, the tune, half time       5
//   bars 25-32   the walls come in under the tune; it climbs        8
//   bars 33-40   the riff, an octave ringing over it               10
//   bars 41-48   the walls, the tune's first words, falling         7
//   bars 49-52   the figure alone                                   2
//
// Chosen on paper with the skill's melody.py: the tune raised no flags; its second half is
// flagged for ending on its top note, which is the point of it (the riff answers). The riff
// is flagged restless, as sevens against four are; the drums under it are as plain as can be.

use engine::drum::{CRASH, Drum, HAT, KICK, OPEN_HAT, RIDE, SNARE}
use engine::guitar::{
    Amp, BASS, CLEAN, DAD_ROCK, Guitar, HUMBUCKER, Hand, LEAD, Picking, SOLO, WALL, pickings,
}
use engine::pattern::{Feel, Pattern, pattern, struck, tacet}
use engine::perform::{Mark, Performance, Taste, bar, perform}
use engine::score::{Meter, Score, meter, score}
use engine::session::{Master, Session, Strip, session}
use std::collections::Vec

pub const TITLE: Text = "Low Sun"
pub const TEMPO: f32 = 88.0
pub const BARS: u32 = 52

fn four() -> Meter {
    meter(beats: 4, unit: 4)
}

fn part(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Score {
    score(TITLE, four()).voice(name, lines)
}

/// `bars` bars of rest for the part `name`.
fn rests(name: Text, bars: u32) -> Score {
    var s = part(name, ["r/1 |"])
    for _ in 1..bars {
        s = take s.then(part(name, ["r/1 |"]))
    }
    s
}

// ---- the notes --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The riff's two bars, each two halves of two beats.
/// The open chord on the beat and again an eighth later, then, on the
/// next beat, the tritone on the low string pushed up a half step to the fifth and held. The
/// next half: the same two strokes and a whole beat of nothing, where the snare is alone.
/// The second bar ends not in nothing but on the chord a half step over home, held a beat.
/// Nothing else: two chords and a bent note, with room round every stroke. And the bar it
/// ends on when what follows is quiet: the first bar again.
const RIFF_1: Text = "<d2 a2 d3>/8 !f !accent <d2 a2 d3>/8 ab2/16t !accent ( a2/8t ~ a2/8 ) <d2 a2 d3>/8 !accent <d2 a2 d3>/8 r/4 |"
const RIFF_2: Text = "<d2 a2 d3>/8 !accent <d2 a2 d3>/8 ab2/16t !accent ( a2/8t ~ a2/8 ) <d2 a2 d3>/8 !accent <d2 a2 d3>/8 <eb2 bb2 eb3>/4 !accent |"
const RIFF_HOLE: Text = "<d2 a2 d3>/8 !accent <d2 a2 d3>/8 ab2/16t !accent ( a2/8t ~ a2/8 ) <d2 a2 d3>/8 !accent <d2 a2 d3>/8 r/4 |"

/// The riff four times over two bars each; the last ends on the hole if `holes`.
fn riff(holes: bool) -> Score {
    var s = part("guitar", [RIFF_1, RIFF_2])
    for k in 1..4 {
        s = take s.then(part("guitar", [RIFF_1, if holes && k == 3 { RIFF_HOLE } else { RIFF_2 }]))
    }
    s
}

/// The driven guitars' whole part: silent, the riff, silent, walls under the tune, the riff,
/// walls, silent.
fn heavy() -> Score {
    var s = rests("guitar", 8)
    s = take s.then(riff(holes: true))
    s = take s.then(rests("guitar", 8))
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "guitar",
            [
                "<bb2 f3 bb3>/1 !mf ~ | <bb2 f3 bb3>/1 | <d2 a2 d3>/1 ~ | <d2 a2 d3>/1 |",
                "<bb2 f3 bb3>/1 ~ | <bb2 f3 bb3>/1 | <c3 g3 c4>/1 !< ~ | <c3 g3 c4>/1 !f |",
            ],
        ),
    )
    s = take s.then(riff(holes: false))
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "guitar",
            [
                "<d2 a2 d3>/1 !f | <bb2 f3 bb3>/1 | <g2 d3 g3>/1 | <d2 a2 d3>/1 |",
                "<d2 a2 d3>/1 !> | <bb2 f3 bb3>/1 | <g2 d3 g3>/1 | <d2 a2 d3>/1 !mp |",
            ],
        ),
    )
    take s.then(rests("guitar", 4))
}

/// The bass under the riff: the riff, an octave under the guitars.
const LOW_1: Text = "d1/8 !f d1 d1/4 d1/8 d1 r/4 |"
const LOW_2: Text = "d1/8 d1 d1/4 d1/8 d1 eb1/4 |"
const LOW_HOLE: Text = "d1/8 d1 d1/4 d1/8 d1 r/4 |"

fn low_riff(holes: bool) -> Score {
    var s = part("bass", [LOW_1, LOW_2])
    for k in 1..4 {
        s = take s.then(part("bass", [LOW_1, if holes && k == 3 { LOW_HOLE } else { LOW_2 }]))
    }
    s
}

/// The bass under the riff and the walls.
fn bass() -> Score {
    var s = rests("bass", 8)
    s = take s.then(low_riff(holes: true))
    s = take s.then(rests("bass", 8))
    // Under the walls: their roots, held as long.
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "bass",
            ["bb1/1 !mf ~ | bb1/1 | d1/1 ~ | d1/1 | bb1/1 ~ | bb1/1 | c2/1 !< ~ | c2/1 !f |"],
        ),
    )
    s = take s.then(low_riff(holes: false))
    s = take s.then(
        part("bass", ["d1/1 !f | bb1/1 | g1/1 | d1/1 | d1/1 !> | bb1/1 | g1/1 | d1/1 !mp |"]),
    )
    take s.then(rests("bass", 4))
}

/// The bass in the quiet: with the figure alone, and under the tune, a line of its own, a
/// root held and a walk to the next. (It is a track of its own, played softly through a
/// cleaner amplifier: on the riff's track, through its driven one, it was as loud as the
/// riff.)
fn bass_line() -> Score {
    var s = rests("bass line", 4)
    s = take s.then(
        part("bass line", ["d2/2. !mp a1/4 | d2/2 c2/4 a1 | bb1/2. f2/4 | bb1/2 r |"]),
    )
    s = take s.then(rests("bass line", 8))
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "bass line",
            [
                "d2/2. !mp a1/4 | d2/2 c2/4 a1 | bb1/2. f2/4 | bb1/2 c2 |",
                "d2/2. a1/4 | d2/2 c2/4 a1 | bb1/2. f2/4 | bb1/1 |",
            ],
        ),
    )
    take s.then(rests("bass line", 28))
}

/// One bar of the figure for each note its top takes: threes against four over the open D
/// and the A above it.
const ROLL_D: Text = "d4/16 a3 d3 d4 a3 d3 d4 a3 d3 d4 a3 d3 d4 a3 d4 a3 |"
const ROLL_E: Text = "e4/16 a3 d3 e4 a3 d3 e4 a3 d3 e4 a3 d3 e4 a3 e4 a3 |"
const ROLL_F: Text = "f4/16 a3 d3 f4 a3 d3 f4 a3 d3 f4 a3 d3 f4 a3 f4 a3 |"
const ROLL_G: Text = "g4/16 a3 d3 g4 a3 d3 g4 a3 d3 g4 a3 d3 g4 a3 g4 a3 |"
const ROLL_A: Text = "a4/16 a3 d3 a4 a3 d3 a4 a3 d3 a4 a3 d3 a4 a3 a4 a3 |"

fn rolls(bars: [Text]) -> Score {
    var s = part("figure", [bars[0]])
    for k in 1..bars.len() {
        s = take s.then(part("figure", [bars[k]]))
    }
    s
}

/// The clean guitar: the figure for eight bars (the last stops halfway, for the riff), silent
/// under the riff, the figure through the tune and the walls, silent under the riff, the
/// figure under the last walls, and alone again, coming to rest on its two fixed notes.
fn figure() -> Score {
    var s = rolls([ROLL_F, ROLL_E, ROLL_F, ROLL_G, ROLL_F, ROLL_E, ROLL_F])
    s = take s.then(part("figure", ["g4/16 !mp a3 d3 g4 a3 d3 g4 a3 r/2 |"]))
    s = take s.then(rests("figure", 8))
    s = take s.then(rolls([ROLL_D, ROLL_D, ROLL_F, ROLL_F, ROLL_D, ROLL_D, ROLL_F, ROLL_A]))
    s = take s.then(rolls([ROLL_F, ROLL_F, ROLL_D, ROLL_D, ROLL_F, ROLL_F, ROLL_E, ROLL_E]))
    s = take s.then(rests("figure", 8))
    s = take s.then(rests("figure", 8))
    s = take s.then(rolls([ROLL_F, ROLL_E, ROLL_F]))
    take s.then(part("figure", ["d4/16 !p a3 d3 a3 d4/2. |"]))
}

/// The held chords, barely driven: D with no third (the tune has the third and the ninth, a
/// half step apart, and says them one at a time), B flat with its major seventh, and C. Over
/// the riff's return, an octave held high: what holds the top while the riff moves under it.
fn wash() -> Score {
    var s = rests("wash", 16)
    for _ in 0..2 {
        s = take s.then(
            part(
                "wash",
                [
                    "<d2 a2 d3 a3 d4>/1 !mp | <d2 a2 d3 a3 d4>/2. <d2 a2 d3 a3 d4>/4 |",
                    "<bb2 f3 a3 d4>/1 | <bb2 f3 a3 d4>/2. <bb2 f3 a3 d4>/4 |",
                ],
            ),
        )
    }
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "wash",
            [
                "<bb2 f3 a3 d4>/1 !mf | <bb2 f3 a3 d4>/1 | <d2 a2 d3 a3 d4>/1 | <d2 a2 d3 a3 d4>/1 |",
                "<bb2 f3 a3 d4>/1 | <bb2 f3 a3 d4>/1 | <c3 g3 c4 e4>/1 | <c3 g3 c4 e4>/1 |",
            ],
        ),
    )
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "wash",
            [
                "<d4 d5>/1 !mf ~ | <d4 d5>/1 | <d4 d5>/1 ~ | <d4 d5>/1 |",
                "<d4 d5>/1 ~ | <d4 d5>/1 | <d4 d5>/1 ~ | <d4 d5>/1 |",
            ],
        ),
    )
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "wash",
            [
                "<d2 a2 d3 a3 d4>/1 !mf | <bb2 f3 a3 d4>/1 | <g2 d3 g3 d4>/1 | <d2 a2 d3 a3 d4>/1 |",
                "<d2 a2 d3 a3 d4>/1 !> | <bb2 f3 a3 d4>/1 | <g2 d3 g3 d4>/1 | <d2 a2 d3 a3 d4>/1 !p |",
            ],
        ),
    )
    take s.then(rests("wash", 4))
}

/// The tune. First: two neighbouring notes, each said twice, long then short; said a step
/// lower over B flat; said again; then a leap of a fourth, an eighth early, held two bars.
/// Then, over the walls: it starts lower and climbs, comes back to its held A, reaches a
/// half step over it, and at the last leaps a fourth to its one highest note and holds it.
/// Last, over the walls falling: its first words, a little changed, and home.
fn tune() -> Score {
    var s = rests("lead", 16)
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "lead",
            [
                "e5/4. !mf e5/8 f5/4. f5/8 | e5/2 r/2 |",
                "d5/4. d5/8 c5/4. c5/8 | d5/2 r/2 |",
                "e5/4. !< e5/8 f5/4. f5/8 | e5/2 r/4. a5/8 !f ~ |",
                "a5/1 ~ | a5/1 |",
            ],
        ),
    )
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "lead",
            [
                "d5/4. !mf d5/8 f5/4. f5/8 | g5/2 r/4 f5/8 g5 |",
                "a5/2. ~ a5/8 g5 | a5/2 r/2 |",
                "bb5/4. !< a5/8 g5/4. f5/8 | g5/2. r/4 |",
                "a5/4. !f a5/8 d6/2 !accent ~ | d6/1 |",
            ],
        ),
    )
    s = take s.then(rests("lead", 8))
    s = take s.then(
        part(
            "lead",
            ["e5/4. !mf e5/8 f5/4. f5/8 | d5/1 | g5/4. !> g5/8 f5/4. f5/8 | d5/1 !p |"],
        ),
    )
    take s.then(rests("lead", 8))
}

// ---- the drums --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The snare tuned up and dried: a higher shell, more of its wires, a short ring.
const CRACK: Drum = Drum {
    tone_hz: 235.0,
    tone_t60: 0.15,
    second_hz: 500.0,
    noise: 1.6,
    noise_t60: 0.2,
    click: 0.2,
    ..SNARE,
}

/// The bass drum for a wall of guitars: a shorter boom and the beater's click, which is what
/// is heard of it through them.
const BEATER: Drum = Drum { tone_hz: 50.0, tone_t60: 0.36, click: 6.0, ..KICK }

/// Two bars of nothing.
const NONE: Text = ".... .... .... .... | .... .... .... .... |"

fn drum(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Pattern {
    pattern(name, four(), lines)
}

/// Two bars written six marks to a beat: the riff's own grid.
fn sixths(name: Text, line: Text) -> Pattern {
    pattern(name, four(), [line], steps: 24)
}

/// Two bars of nothing, six marks to a beat.
const NONE_SIXTHS: Text = "...... ...... ...... ...... | ...... ...... ...... ...... |"

/// A drum's whole part, each two bars four times over: silent for eight bars, `riff`, `soft`
/// (under the tune), `full` (under the tune and the walls), `again` (the riff's return,
/// harder), `wide` (under the last walls), and silent for four.
fn kit(name: Text, riff: Text, soft: Text, full: Text, again: Text, wide: Text) -> Pattern {
    var p = tacet(four(), bars: 8)
    p = take p.then(sixths(name, riff).times(4))
    p = take p.then(drum(name, [soft]).times(4))
    p = take p.then(drum(name, [full]).times(4))
    p = take p.then(sixths(name, again).times(4))
    p = take p.then(drum(name, [wide]).times(4))
    take p.then(tacet(four(), bars: 4))
}

// ---- the session ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// A score as the player `seed` plays it: accents leaned on, no two notes quite alike.
fn played(s: Score, seed: u32) -> Performance {
    perform(
        s,
        Taste {
            tempo: TEMPO,
            metre: 0.04,
            accent: 0.3,
            jitter_time: 0.004,
            jitter_velocity: 0.06,
            seed,
        },
        [Mark::Hold { at: bar(1), by: 1.0 }; 0],
    )
}

/// Drop D: the lowest string a whole step down, so one finger across the low three strings
/// is a chord of a fifth.
const DROP_D: [f32; 6] = [38.0, 45.0, 50.0, 55.0, 59.0, 64.0]
const BASS_DROP_D: [f32; 6] = [26.0, 33.0, 38.0, 43.0, 47.0, 52.0]

/// The whole piece, ready to play.
pub fn build() -> Session {
    // The master is driven gently: the drums' hits are what the limiter would flatten first.
    var s = session(
        TEMPO,
        Master {
            gain: 0.0,
            glue_db: -18.0,
            glue: 0.25,
            makeup: 2.5,
            warmth: 0.6,
            ceiling: -1.0,
            room_time: 1.1,
            room_highs: 0.4,
            room_size: 1.8,
            room_db: -7.0,
            echo_beats: 0.75,
            echo_again: 0.35,
            echo_db: -6.0,
            duck_time: 0.07,
        },
    )
    // The drums. Under the riff: the bass drum on the open chord's two strokes and nowhere
    // else, a crash on the bar's first, an open hi-hat every eighth, and the snare on the
    // second and fourth beats: with the bent note the first time, alone in the silence the
    // second. When the riff returns the bass drum adds a pickup and the snare a roll into
    // each second bar. Under the tune: half as busy, on the ride; under the walls, fuller.
    let feel = Feel { loose: 0.002, uneven: 0.05, seed: 3 }
    s.drum(
        "kick",
        BEATER,
        struck(
            kit(
                "kick",
                "x..x.. ...... x..x.. ...... | x..x.. ...... x..x.. .....x |",
                "x... .... ..x. .... | x... .... .x.. .... |",
                "x... ..x. .... x... | x... ..x. .... x.x. |",
                "x..x.. ...... x..x.. .....x | x..x.. ...... x..x.. ...x.x |",
                "x... .... ..x. .... | x... ..x. .... .... |",
            ),
            TEMPO,
            feel,
            key: 36,
        ),
        Strip { gain: 6.0, room: 0.05 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "snare",
        CRACK,
        struck(
            kit(
                "snare",
                "...... X..... ...... X..... | ...... X..... ...... X..... |",
                ".... .... x... .... | .... .... x... ...o |",
                ".... .... X... .... | .... .... X... ..o. |",
                "...... X..... ...... X..... | ...... X..... ...... X..xxx |",
                ".... .... X... .... | .... .... X... .... |",
            ),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { late: 0.006, ..feel },
            key: 38,
        ),
        Strip { gain: 6.5, room: 0.12 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "open hat",
        OPEN_HAT,
        struck(
            kit(
                "open hat",
                "x..x.. x..x.. x..x.. x..x.. | x..x.. x..x.. x..x.. x..x.. |",
                NONE,
                NONE,
                "x..x.. x..x.. x..x.. x..x.. | x..x.. x..x.. x..x.. x..x.. |",
                NONE,
            ),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { late: -0.004, ..feel },
            key: 46,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -1.0, pan: 0.3, low_cut: 400.0, room: 0.15 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "ride",
        RIDE,
        struck(
            kit(
                "ride",
                NONE_SIXTHS,
                "x... x... x... x... | x... x... x... x.x. |",
                "x... x... x... x... | x... x... x... x.x. |",
                NONE_SIXTHS,
                "x... x... x... x... | x... x... x... x... |",
            ),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { late: -0.003, ..feel },
            key: 51,
        ),
        Strip { gain: 0.0, pan: -0.25, low_cut: 300.0, room: 0.25 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "crash",
        CRASH,
        struck(
            kit(
                "crash",
                "X..... ...... ...... ...... | ...... ...... ...... ...... |",
                "x... .... .... .... | .... .... .... .... |",
                "X... .... .... .... | .... .... .... .... |",
                "X..... ...... ...... ...... | X..... ...... ...... ...... |",
                "X... .... .... .... | x... .... .... .... |",
            ),
            TEMPO,
            feel,
            key: 49,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -7.0, pan: -0.3, low_cut: 300.0, room: 0.3 },
    )
    // The bass guitar: in the middle, pushed down a little by each bass drum. Its amplifier
    // driven a little harder and its speaker opened up, so its growl at 700 Hz to 2 kHz is
    // heard through the guitars and not only its bottom felt under them.
    let growl = Amp { drive: 19.0, mid: 1.3, treble: 1.3, cab_high: 3600.0, ..BASS.amp }
    let low = Guitar { open: BASS_DROP_D, amp: growl, ..BASS }
    let b = bass()
    s.guitar(
        "bass",
        low,
        pickings(b, played(b, 5), 0, low, Hand { mutes: false }),
        Strip { gain: 0.5, high_cut: 4500.0, duck: 3.0, room: 0.03 },
    )
    let soft = Guitar { open: BASS_DROP_D, ..BASS }
    let bl = bass_line()
    s.guitar(
        "bass line",
        soft,
        pickings(bl, played(bl, 6), 0, soft, Hand { mutes: false }),
        Strip { gain: -6.0, high_cut: 3000.0, duck: 2.0, room: 0.05 },
    )
    // The riff and the walls: two players, one a side, through two speakers, each pushed
    // down a little by the bass drum.
    // The wall's amplifier with fewer of the lows cut before its valves: there are no fast
    // chugs to keep apart now, and the weight is under 80 Hz.
    let tight = Amp { tight: 120.0, ..WALL }
    let left = Guitar { open: DROP_D, amp: tight, ..HUMBUCKER }
    let right = Guitar { open: DROP_D, amp: Amp { cone: 29, ..tight }, ..HUMBUCKER }
    let h = heavy()
    // Every stroke down; a slur of a half step on one string is a bend.
    let down = Hand { up_every: 0, strum: 0.005, bends: 1, bend_time: 0.24 }
    s.guitar(
        "guitar left",
        left,
        pickings(h, played(h, 11), 0, left, down),
        Strip { gain: -6.0, pan: -0.92, low_cut: 100.0, duck: 1.5, room: 0.12 },
    )
    s.guitar(
        "guitar right",
        right,
        pickings(h, played(h, 12), 0, right, down),
        Strip { gain: -6.0, pan: 0.92, low_cut: 100.0, duck: 1.5, room: 0.12 },
    )
    // The held chords: barely driven, far back and wide.
    let hazy = Guitar {
        open: DROP_D,
        amp: Amp { drive: 9.0, level: -14.0, ..DAD_ROCK },
        ..HUMBUCKER,
    }
    let w = wash()
    let slow = Hand { up_every: 0, strum: 0.02, ring: 0.6 }
    s.guitar(
        "wash left",
        hazy,
        pickings(w, played(w, 21), 0, hazy, slow),
        Strip { gain: 1.5, pan: -0.85, low_cut: 110.0, room: 0.4, echo: 0.15 },
    )
    s.guitar(
        "wash right",
        Guitar { amp: Amp { cone: 41, ..hazy.amp }, ..hazy },
        pickings(w, played(w, 22), 0, hazy, slow),
        Strip { gain: 1.5, pan: 0.85, low_cut: 110.0, room: 0.4, echo: 0.15 },
    )
    // The figure: clean, each string let ring, its echo a dotted eighth behind.
    let clean = Guitar { open: DROP_D, ..CLEAN }
    let f = figure()
    s.guitar(
        "figure",
        clean,
        pickings(f, played(f, 31), 0, clean, Hand { ring: 1.0 }),
        Strip { gain: -1.0, pan: -0.15, low_cut: 100.0, room: 0.3, echo: 0.4 },
    )
    // The tune: a lead guitar, in front, a little echo.
    let singer = Guitar { open: DROP_D, ..LEAD }
    let t = tune()
    s.guitar(
        "lead",
        singer,
        pickings(t, played(t, 41), 0, singer, SOLO),
        Strip { gain: -4.0, pan: 0.1, low_cut: 150.0, room: 0.2, echo: 0.3 },
    )
    s.key("kick")
    s
}
